{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/711861-m-tc-soundtrack-ideas","id":711861,"title":"M:tC Soundtrack ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-20T23:00:47-07:00","id":711861,"title":"M:tC Soundtrack ideas","content":"I'm looking for some good ideas for a soundtrack for a Mummy game. Strangely, Mummies get little love and it's actually hard to find appropriate music. <br /> Obviously, I'm hoping for something deeper than the soundtrack for the Brendan Fraser movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5323-nyarlathotep5150","name":"Nyarlathotep5150","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T00:27:27-07:00","id":711984,"title":"","content":"I'm a sucker for the Stargate theme :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T05:38:05-07:00","id":712273,"title":"","content":"My two go-to soundtracks are the Fountain and Noah. I believe both are by the same composer. The Fountain is my default for romance, tragedy, memory, and apotheosis, with a few songs I've consistently used as the Dreams of Avarice theme song. Noah is a dark and moody soundtrack, good for those feelings of ancient dread. I've use Noah for a lot of the horror aspects of the Rite of Return, the Judges, Irem.. either way, both soundtracks have a timeless, ancient feel to them, but can get nostalgic. There's even some continuity between them, if you listen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T15:01:25-07:00","id":713067,"title":"","content":"Darude: sandstorm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T21:16:12-07:00","id":713662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/711861-m-tc-soundtrack-ideas?p=713067#post713067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Darude: sandstorm</div> </div> </div> </div>At first I thought, &quot;Heh, classic.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then I got it. Kudos for you.","sign